<title>BELGIUM: Belgian money market supply raised in week.</title>
<headline>Belgian money market supply raised in week.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Belgian central bank said it added liquidity to the money market in the week to Monday to offset a seasonal rise in notes in circulation.</p>
<p>(figures from the weekly statement in bln francs) -</p>
<p> Foreign currency reserves	   448.256 (+ 0.456)</p>
<p>Advances against pledged security  17.763 (- 3.894)</p>
<p> Commercial bills			  2.336 (- 0.025)</p>
<p> Securities portfolio		   25.795 (+ 0.000)</p>
<p> Money market interventions*	 121.756 (+ 7.044)</p>
<p> Bank notes in circulation	   484.340 (+ 1.876)</p>
<p>* comprises repurchase agreements and interbank loans</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
